API Documentation
This document provides a comprehensive overview of the RESTful API endpoints for the Laravel Assessment Project.

1.	Authentication
1.1 Register User
    Endpoint:
        POST /api/register
    Request Body:
        {
            "first_name": "",
            "last_name": "",
            "email": "",
            "password": ""
        }
    Response:
        Returns the token.

1.2 Login User
    Endpoint:
        POST /api/login
    Request Body:
        {
            "email": "",
            "password": ""
        }
    Response:
        Returns the token.

1.3 Logout User
    Endpoint:
        POST /api/logout
    Headers:
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json
    Response:
        {
            "message": "Successfully logged out"
        }

2. Attributes

2.1 Create Attribute
    Endpoint:
        POST /api/attributes
    Headers:
        Content-Type: application/json
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json
    Request Body:
        {
            "name": "",
            "type": ""
        }
    Response:
        Returns the created attribute.

2.2 List Attributes
    Endpoint:
        GET /api/attributes
    Headers:
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json
    Response:
        Returns a list of all dynamic attributes.
        
2.3 Update Attribute
    Endpoint:
        PUT /api/attributes/{id}
    Headers:
        Content-Type: application/json
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json
    Request Body:
        {
            "name": "",
            "type": ""
        }
    Response:
        Returns the updated attribute.

2.4 Delete Attribute
    Endpoint:
        DELETE /api/attributes/{id}
    Headers:
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json
    Response:
        {
            "message": "Attribute deleted successfully"
        }

3. Projects

3.1 Create Project
    Endpoint:
        POST /api/projects
    Headers:
        Content-Type: application/json
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json
    Request Body:
        {
        "name": "",
        "status": "",
        "attributes": {
            "attribute_id": "value",       
            }
        }
    Response:
        Returns the created project.

3.2 List Projects
    Endpoint:
        GET /api/projects
    Headers:
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json    
    Response:
        Returns a list of projects with their dynamic attributes.

3.3 Get Project Detail
    Endpoint:
        GET /api/projects/{id}
    Headers:
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json
    Response:
        Returns the project details for the specified project ID.

3.4 Update Project
    Endpoint:
        PUT /api/projects/{id}
    Headers:
        Content-Type: application/json
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json
    Request Body:
        {
            "name": "Updated Project Name",
            "status": "inactive",
            "attributes": {
                "1": "Marketing",
                "2": "2025-04-01"
            }
        }
    Response:
        Returns the updated project details.

3.5 Delete Project
    Endpoint:
        DELETE /api/projects/{id}
    Headers:
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json
    Response:
        {
            "message": "Project deleted successfully"
        }

3.6 Filter Projects
    Endpoint:
        GET /api/projects?filters[name]=like:ProjectA&filters[department]=IT
    Headers:
        Authorization: Bearer <Token>
        Accept: application/json
    Response:
    Returns a list of projects that match the filter criteria.

3.7 Project-User Assignment
    Endpoint:
        POST /api/projects/{id}/users
    Headers:
        Content-Type: application/json
        Accept: application/json
        Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_TOKEN_HERE>
    Request Body:
        {
        "user_id": id
        }
    Response:
        {
        "message": "User added to project successfully"
        }

